Package: specdiv
Title: Uncertainty-Aware Taxonomic, Phylogenetic and Functional Diversity from Predicted Species
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Nathan G.", "Swenson", email = "nswenson@nd.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A nondestructive, uncertainty-aware framework for estimating the
    taxonomic, phylogenetic and functional diversity of an assemblage from
    per-individual species predictions rather than hard identifications. A
    calibrated probabilistic classifier assigns each individual a probability
    vector over candidate species; a Monte Carlo repeatedly draws identities,
    reconstitutes each site, and recomputes diversity, so every per-site estimate
    carries a confidence interval. All three axes are returned as Hill numbers of
    matched order (a common "effective number of species" currency), together with
    standardized effect sizes of assemblage structure. The engine is agnostic to
    how the probabilities arise; a spectral front-end (leaf-clip reflectance,
    PLS-DA) is provided for the leaf-spectroscopy case for which the framework was
    developed, along with helpers for cross-campaign batch alignment and an
    independent abundance prior for the open-species-pool setting.
